cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this teaching ebook, please cite it as below."
title: "Bayesian Clinical Reasoning: Statistics, Decision Analysis, and Evidence for Neurologists and Clinician-Scientists"
abstract: >-
  Open-source teaching ebook on Bayesian clinical reasoning for neurology and
  related specialties. Twenty chapters move from probability language and Bayes'
  theorem through hierarchical models in R (brms) to decision analysis, net
  benefit, and shared decision-making. Educational only — not medical advice,
  not local policy, not institutional endorsement.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kalani
    given-names: Rizwan
url: "https://rkalani1.github.io/bayesian-clinical-reasoning/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rkalani1/bayesian-clinical-reasoning"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Bayesian statistics
  - clinical reasoning
  - decision analysis
  - neurology
  - stroke
  - medical education
  - brms
  - evidence-based medicine
